{"study_accession":"PRJNA483024","secondary_study_accession":"SRP155381","title":"A stably self-renewing adult blood-derived induced neural stem cell exhibiting patternability and epigenetic rejuvenation","description":"Recent reports suggest that induced neurons (iNs), but not induced pluripotent stem cell (iPSC)-derived neurons largely preserve age-associated traits. Here we report on the extent of preserved epigenetic and transcriptional aging signatures in directly converted induced neural stem cells (iNSCs). Employing restricted and integration-free expression of SOX2 and c-MYC we generate a fully functional, bona fide NSC population from adult blood cells that remains highly responsive to regional patterning cues. Upon conversion, low passage iNSCs display a profound loss of age-related DNA methylation signatures, which further erode across extended passaging, thereby approximating the DNA methylation age of isogenic iPSC-derived neural precursors. This epigenetic rejuvenation is accompanied by a lack of age-associated transcriptional signatures and absence of cellular aging hallmarks. We find iNSCs to be competent for modeling pathological protein aggregation and for neurotransplantation, depicting blood-to-NSC conversion as a rapid alternative route for both disease modeling and neuroregeneration. Overall design: 19 human cell samples representing either EPC, iNSC or smNPC were used for identification of differentially expressed genes by RNAseq","pubmed":"30279449","geo_series":"","n_samples":11,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN09724480","study_accession":"PRJNA483024","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"study","title":"R913:_smNPC_MJD33b_P6","description":"R913:_smNPC_MJD33b_P6","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3307709","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2018-11-10","attributes":[["source_name","R913: smNPC MJD33b P6"],["cell_type","smNPC"],["donor","MJD33b"],["passage","P6"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR7608395","experiment_accession"